# Everything a run produces. These are outputs, not sources: the warrant ids
# change on every run, and committing them would make each demo a diff.
warrant-training.json
warrant-execution.json
refusal-*.json
generation.json
# Anything else a run drops beside a build script. The list above kept
# growing one name at a time — a warrant, then a refusal, then a
# generation — so the rule is now the shape rather than the names.
*/*-record.json
*.tex
*.pdf
*.aux
*.log
*.out

# The Ames data is third-party and downloaded on first run. It belongs to its
# publisher, it is a megabyte, and the script fetches it from the authoritative
# URL — a copy in here would be exactly the convenient mirror the README argues
# against.
02_home_price_regression/data/
